        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(signal): surface daemon errors split across output chunks",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Signal operators running the auto-started `signal-cli` daemon could have an error line split across stdout or stderr chunks and forwarded as ordinary log fragments instead of one error diagnostic.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe shared Signal daemon output boundary now reads complete lines before applying the existing log classifier. This covers both stdout and stderr, preserves CRLF and LF input plus a final unterminated line, and does not change daemon lifecycle, configuration, or channel delivery behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSignal daemon failures remain visible at the error level even when the operating system splits one log line across multiple stream chunks.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: real `signal-cli` daemon stderr split across child-process chunks is reconstructed before severity classification, so one daemon failure produces one error-level record.\n- Current head: `9ea914269198d773adabe2a896ba16e4a78d3b06`.\n- Real-daemon setup: OpenClaw's `spawnSignalDaemon` launched the official JVM release `signal-cli 0.14.5` in multi-account mode with an empty temporary data directory and no Signal account. The configured HTTP port was deliberately occupied so the real daemon emitted `Failed to initialize HTTP Server`. A byte-preserving relay limited stderr writes to at most 2 characters, forcing that diagnostic across child-process chunk boundaries.\n- Redacted terminal transcript:\n\n  ```text\n  signal-cli version: signal-cli 0.14.5\n  transport fault: stderr relayed in writes of at most 2 characters\n  matching error-level records: 1\n  signal-cli: Failed to initialize HTTP Server\n  ```\n\n- Focused regression: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/signal/src/daemon.test.ts` passed all 5 tests.\n- Targeted format: `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check extensions/signal/src/daemon.ts extensions/signal/src/daemon.test.ts` passed.\n- Diff hygiene: `git diff --check HEAD~1..HEAD` passed.\n- Autoreview: `python .agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local` completed with no accepted/actionable findings.\n\n",
